Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 04:23:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/46] Move the tab switcher toolbar to the bottom

The tab switcher kept its new tab and menu buttons at the top while the browsing
toolbar sits at the bottom, so the two modes disagreed and the buttons were a
long reach on a large phone.

Chromium already implements a bottom toolbar for the hub, in
HubBottomToolbarCoordinator and HubBottomBarBottomToolbarDelegateImpl, but
HubBottomToolbarDelegateFactory gates it behind two checks that are both off by
default: the ANDROID_BOTTOM_BAR feature, disabled on both the native and Java
side, and its show_bottom_bar_on_gts parameter. Enabling all three is enough; no
layout changes were needed.

The tab, grid and history control stays at the top. Only the new tab and menu
buttons move down, which is what makes the two modes agree.

Verified on device: no crashes, and the Ask Gemini button removed in patch 0019
does not return, which was the risk in enabling this subsystem.
---
 chrome/browser/flags/android/chrome_feature_list.cc           | 2 +-
 .../org/chromium/chrome/browser/flags/ChromeFeatureList.java  | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/flags/android/chrome_feature_list.cc b/chrome/browser/flags/android/chrome_feature_list.cc
index 0b99265877..f47ccb7573 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/flags/android/chrome_feature_list.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/flags/android/chrome_feature_list.cc
@@ -621,7 +621,7 @@ BASE_FEATURE(kAndroidActorTaskTimeout, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 BASE_FEATURE(kAndroidAppIntegrationMultiDataSource, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 BASE_FEATURE(kAndroidAppRatingPrompt, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 BASE_FEATURE(kAndroidAtomsLogging, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
-BASE_FEATURE(kAndroidBottomBar, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+BASE_FEATURE(kAndroidBottomBar, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 BASE_FEATURE(kAndroidBottomBarAim, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 BASE_FEATURE(kAndroidBricksNativePage, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 BASE_FEATURE(kAndroidContextMenuDisabledMenuItems, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
diff --git a/chrome/browser/flags/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/flags/ChromeFeatureList.java b/chrome/browser/flags/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/flags/ChromeFeatureList.java
